# WSMath — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development, or set these in the host's project
# settings. Everything here is public: `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined into
# the static export at build time, so never put a secret in this file.

# Where WhatsApp CTA clicks are reported.
#
# Every conversion on this site is a `wa.me` deep link and there is no other
# funnel, so which section and which package drives an enquiry is the one
# question the business has never been able to answer (editor contract §7).
#
# `src/lib/cta-beacon.ts` posts `{ site, cta, path, referrer, ts }` here with
# `navigator.sendBeacon` on every CTA click. The endpoint will live in the
# editor, which already has the database; until it exists, leave this
# unset — the beacon is a silent no-op and never throws or blocks a click.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CTA_ENDPOINT=https://example.com/api/cta
NEXT_PUBLIC_CTA_ENDPOINT=

# Which origin may post a draft into /preview.
#
# The editor frames `/preview` and posts the twelve content documents
# in with `postMessage` (editor contract §3.3). Set this to the editor's origin and the
# listener accepts drafts from it and nothing else.
#
# Leave it unset (or empty) and any origin may post — which is what the current
# editor-less workflow needs, and why the default is permissive. Set it before
# the editor ships: without it, any page that can reach this frame can repaint
# the preview with content that will never deploy.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EDITOR_ORIGIN=https://editor.example.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_EDITOR_ORIGIN=
